"Before The Gates of a Granite Structure"
"A great wall of granite rises to the north, at least thirty feet high, forming

the outside of a grand structure.  To the east and west stand two rounded

towers with cone-shaped roofs.  Fixed into the wall just north of you is a

large gate which seeming leads into the granite structure beyond the grand

walls.  Overhead a large banner can be seen.

