#85012
"Great Library"
"The library is a large semi-circular room of polished granite.  In the center

is a blazing fire place that lends both warmth and good light for reading. 

Along the straight wall are shelves upon shelves stacked floor to ceiling with

unbelievable volumes of literature, from the most common, to the most rare. 

This is one of the most extensive private collections you have ever seen,

rivaling many town libraries.  Skirting the the rounded part of the room are

many chairs and couches, not the hard wooden kinds you might see in taverns,

but comfortable hand crafted pieces of furniture collected from many regions. 

Covered in unusual fabrics and stuffed with soft cottons and animal furrs,

they lend themselves to a cozy place to curl up with a good book for a little

rest and relaxation after a hard fought campaign in the name of the light.

"
""
